"The Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order (https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.6549)\nciteturn3academia1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.0 years ago; Title: The Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order ... In 2012 Jan Saxl conjectured that all irreducible representations of the symmetric group occur in the decomposition of the tensor square of the irreducible representation corresponding to the staircase partition.\nTitle: The Saxl Conjecture and the Dominance Order\nAuthors: Christian Ikenmeyer\nDate: Fri Oct 24 02:51:48 2014\n\nIn 2012 Jan Saxl conjectured that all irreducible representations of the symmetric group occur in the decomposition of the tensor square of the irreducible representation corresponding to the staircase partition. We make progress on this conjecture by proving the occurrence of all those irreducibles which correspond to partitions that are comparable to the staircase partition in the dominance order. Moreover, we use our result to show the occurrence of all irreducibles corresponding to hook partitions. This generalizes results by Pak, Panova, and Vallejo from 2013.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSplitting Kronecker squares, 2-decomposition numbers, Catalan combinatorics, and the Saxl conjecture (https://alco.centre-mersenne.org/articles/10.5802/alco.294/)\nciteturn3search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.1 years ago; Crawled: last week; Splitting Kronecker squares, 2-decomposition numbers, Catalan combinatorics, and the Saxl conjecture ... [34] Mészáros, Szabolcs; Wolosz, János Symmetric and exterior squares of hook representations, 2019 | arXiv ... [43] Saxl, Jan The complex characters of the symmetric groups that remain irreducible in subgroups, J.\n\nSplitting Kronecker squares, 2-decomposition numbers, Catalan combinatorics, and the Saxl conjecture\n\nBessenrodt, Christine; Bowman, Chris^{1}\n\n^{1}Department of Mathematics University of York Heslington, York, YO10 5DD United Kingdom\n\nAlgebraic Combinatorics, Volume 6 (2023) no. 4, pp. 863-899\n\nThis paper concerns the symmetric and anti-symmetric Kronecker products of characters of the symmetric groups. We provide new closed formulas for decomposing these products, unexpected connections with 2-modular decomposition numbers, Catalan combinatorics, and a refinement of the famous Saxl conjecture.\n\nReceived: 2022-06-05\nRevised: 2023-01-10\nAccepted: 2023-01-13\nPublished online: 2023-08-29\n\nDOI: 10.5802/alco.294\n\nClassification: 05A05, 05A10, 05E05, 05A15, 05E10, 05E16, 81Q30\nKeywords: Symmetric tensor squares, Kronecker product, symmetric groups, character theory, decomposition numbers, Catalan combinatorics.\n\nAuthor's affiliations:\n\nBessenrodt, Christine  ^{ } ; Bowman, Chris  ^{ 1 }\n\n^{1} Department of Mathematics University of York Heslington, York, YO10 5DD United Kingdom\n\nLicense: Image CC-BY 4.0\n\nCopyrights: The authors retain unrestricted copyrights and publishing rights\n    \n    Bessenrodt, Christine; Bowman, Chris. Splitting Kronecker squares, 2-decomposition numbers, Catalan combinatorics, and the Saxl conjecture. Algebraic Combinatorics, Volume 6 (2023) no. 4, pp. 863-899. doi: 10.5802/alco.294\n\n[1] Ballantine, Cristina M.; Orellana, Rosa C. A combinatorial interpretation for the coefficients in the Kronecker product {s}_{(n-p,p)}*{s}_{\\lambda }, Sém. Lothar. Combin., Volume 54A (2005/07), Paper no. B54Af, 29 pages | MR | Zbl\n\n[9] Bürgisser, Peter; Christandl, Matthias; Ikenmeyer, Christian Nonvanishing of Kronecker coefficients for rectangular shapes, Adv. Math., Volume 227 (2011) no. 5, pp. 2082-2091 | MR | Zbl | DOI\n\n[10] Bürgisser, Peter; Ikenmeyer, Christian; Hüttenhain, Jesko Permanent versus determinant: not via saturations, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc., Volume 145 (2017) no. 3, pp. 1247-1258 | Zbl | MR | DOI\n\n[11] Bürgisser, Peter; Ikenmeyer, Christian; Panova, Greta No occurrence obstructions in geometric complexity theory, J. Amer. Math. Soc., Volume 32 (2019) 