n finite group representation theory, Cambridge Studies in Advanced Mathematics, 161, Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, 2016, xi+325 pages | MR | DOI\n\n[51] Wolosz, János Irreducible modules for symmetric groups that are summands of their exterior square, J. Algebra, Volume 518 (2019), pp. 304-320 | Zbl | MR | DOI\n\n[52] Zisser, Ilan The character covering numbers of the alternating groups, J. Algebra, Volume 153 (1992) no. 2, pp. 357-372 | Zbl | MR | DOI--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGeneration by conjugate elements of finite almost simple groups with a sporadic socle (https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03673)\nciteturn3academia2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.7 years ago; Date: Tue Feb  6 03:51:27 2024 ... The outcome of this paper together with one by Di Martino, Pellegrini, and Zalesski, both of which are based on computer calculations with character tables, is a refinement of the estimates by Guralnick and Saxl on the value of $\\alpha_S(x)$ in the case where $S$ is a sporadic group.\nTitle: Generation by conjugate elements of finite almost simple groups with a sporadic socle\nAuthors: Danila O. Revin, Andrei V. Zavarnitsine\nDate: Tue Feb  6 03:51:27 2024\n\nAs defined by Guralnick and Saxl given a nonabelian simple group $S$ and its nonidentity automorphism $x$, a natural number $\\alpha_S(x)$ does not exceed a natural number $m$ if some $m$ conjugates of $x$ in the group $\\langle x,S\\rangle$ generate a subgroup that includes $S$. The outcome of this paper together with one by Di Martino, Pellegrini, and Zalesski, both of which are based on computer calculations with character tables, is a refinement of the estimates by Guralnick and Saxl on the value of $\\alpha_S(x)$ in the case where $S$ is a sporadic group. In particular, we prove that $\\alpha_S(x)\\leqslant 4$, except when $S$ is one of the Fischer groups and $x$ is a $3$-transposition. In the latter case, $\\alpha_S(x)=6$ if $S$ is either $Fi_{22}$ or $Fi_{23}$ and $\\alpha_S(x)=5$ if $S={Fi_{24}}'$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nALGEBRAIC\nCOMBINATORICS\nChristine Bessenrodt & Chr (https://alco.centre-mersenne.org/item/10.5802/alco.294.pdf)\nciteturn3search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; [43] Jan Saxl, The complex characters of the symmetric groups that remain irreducible in subgroups, ... [51] János Wolosz, Irreducible modules for symmetric groups that are summands of their exterior\nSplitting Kronecker squares\n[41] Nicolas Ressayre, Vanishing symmetric Kronecker coefficients, Beitr. Algebra Geom. 61 (2020),\nno. 2, 231–246.\n[42] Mercedes H. Rosas, The Kronecker product of Schur functions indexed by two-row shapes or\nhook shapes, J. Algebraic Combin. 14 (2001), no. 2, 153–173.\n[43] Jan Saxl, The complex characters of the symmetric groups that remain irreducible in subgroups,\nJ. Algebra 111 (1987), no. 1, 210–219.\n[44] Jean-Pierre Serre, Linear representations of finite groups, french ed., Graduate Texts in Math-\nematics, vol. 42, Springer-Verlag, New York-Heidelberg, 1977.\n[45] Boyan Sirakov, Paulo Ney de Souza, and Marcelo Viana (eds.), Proceedings of the International\nCongress of Mathematicians—Rio de Janeiro 2018. Vol. I. Plenary lectures, World Scientific\nPublishing Co. Pte. Ltd., Hackensack, NJ, 2018, ICM 2018, August 1–9, 2018.\n[46] Richard P. Stanley, Positivity problems and conjectures in algebraic combinatorics, in Mathe-\nmatics: frontiers and perspectives, Amer. Math. Soc., Providence, RI, 2000, pp. 295–319.\n[47] Jay Taylor, A note on skew characters of symmetric groups, Israel J. Math. 221 (2017), no. 1,\n435–443.\n[48] R. M. Thrall, On symmetrized Kronecker powers and the structure of the free Lie ring, Amer.\nJ. Math. 64 (1942), 371–388.\n[49] Ernesto Vallejo, A diagrammatic approach to Kronecker squares, J. Combin. Theory Ser. A 127\n(2014), 243–285.\n[50] Peter Webb, A course in finite group representation theory, Cambridge Studies in Advanced\nMathematics, vol. 161, Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, 2016.\n[51] János Wolosz, Irreducible modules for symmetric groups that are summands of their exterior\nsquare, J. Algebra 518 (2019), 304–320.\n[52] Ilan Zisser, The character covering numbers of the alternating groups, J. Algebra 153 (1992),\nno. 2, 357–372.\nChristine Bessenrodt\nChris Bowman, Department of Mathematics, University of York, Heslington, York, YO10 5DD,\nUnited Kingdom\nE-mail : chris.bowman-scargill@york.ac.uk\nAlgebraic Combinatorics, Vol. 6 #4 (2023)\n899"
